  "solution": "**Given:**\n\n(189, 148, 107)\n\n(206, 165, 124)\n\n**Logic**: [(First no. - Second no.) = (Second no. - Third no.)]\n\n**(189, 148, 107) →**\n\n⇒ [(189 - 148) = (148 - 107)]\n\n⇒ [41 = 41]\n\n**(206, 165, 124) →**\n\n⇒ [(206 - 165) = (165 - 124)]\n\n⇒ [41 = 41]\n\nChecking all the given options:\n\n**1.** (84, 67, 39)\n\n⇒ [(84 - 67) = (67 - 39)]\n\n⇒ [17 = 28]\n\n**2.** (121, 85, 45)\n\n⇒ [(121 - 85) = (85 - 45)]\n\n⇒ [36 = 40]\n\n**3.** (76, 46, 26)\n\n⇒ [(76 - 46) = (46 - 26)]\n\n⇒ [30 = 20]\n\n**4. (108, 67, 26)**\n\n⇒ [(108 - 67) = (67 - 26)]\n\n⇒ [41 = 41]\n\nHere, **(108, 67, 26)** shows a similar relation to the given set of numbers.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"Option (4)\".",
